## 2. WAI-ARIA tabs pattern (points 3, 9)
Structural check (manual.js, `STRUCT` output) on the rendered page:
- `<div role="tablist" aria-label="Supporting charts and tables">` — accessible name present.
- 5× `<button role="tab" id="insights-tab-{key}" aria-controls="insights-panel-{key}"
  aria-selected>` — every `aria-controls` resolves to a real panel id (verified in
  render_insights_lt6_test.go too, `go test ./internal/templates/... -run
  TestRenderInsightsSupportingTabs -v` → PASS).
- 5× `<div role="tabpanel" id="insights-panel-{key}" aria-labelledby="insights-tab-{key}"
  tabindex="0">` — every `aria-labelledby` resolves to a real tab id.
- Roving tabindex confirmed live: default state trends tab `tabindex=0`, other 4 at `-1`;
  after Home/End/Arrow moves, exactly one tab is `tabindex=0` at all times (ROVING TABINDEX
  dump in manual.js output).
- Keyboard trace: ArrowRight from `insights-tab-trends` → focus AND activation moved to
  `insights-tab-income` (`aria-selected=true`, `insights-panel-income.hidden=false`,
  `insights-panel-trends.hidden=true`); End → `insights-tab-pace` focused+selected; Home →
  `insights-tab-trends`; Enter on a focused-but-inactive tab (`anomalies`) activated it
  (`aria-selected=true`, panel unhidden). Click and Space are implemented identically in
  insights.js (web/static/js/insights.js:396-401, keydown handler checks
  `'Enter' || ' ' || 'Spacebar'`).
- Tab key from the active tab (`insights-tab-trends`, focused via Home) landed
  `document.activeElement` INSIDE `insights-panel-trends` (ancestorPanelId matched) — not
  on a hidden panel's content, confirming hidden panels (native `hidden` attribute) are
  correctly removed from both the accessibility tree and the tab order.
- Focus-visible outline present in both themes on `[data-ins-tab]:focus-visible`
  (styles.css:225, added alongside the existing `[data-wf-tab]:focus-visible` rule — reuses
  the same theme-aware outline, no new color introduced): light `rgb(79,70,229)` solid 2px,
  dark `rgb(165,180,252)` solid 2px. Contrast vs the real computed body background
  (`rgb(243,244,246)` light / `rgb(17,24,39)` dark, measured live via getComputedStyle, not
  assumed): light 5.71:1, dark 8.90:1 — both ≫ 3:1 (point 7 UI-component clause).
- Active-vs-inactive distinguishable by more than color (point 8): inactive tabs carry
  `border-b-2 border-transparent`; the active tab's `.wf-tab-active` class (JS-toggled, same
  class already used and accepted for What-If tabs) sets `border-bottom-color` to the same
  indigo as the text — an underline appears/disappears, not just a text-color swap. This is
  the pre-existing, already-accepted What-If tab convention (styles.css:213-220), reused
  verbatim per ruling LT-2026-09-07d.

## 3. Contrast, points 7/12, both themes, incl. hover
Live computed colors (colors.js), fed through WCAG relative-luminance contrast:
- Inactive tab text `rgb(75,85,99)`(light)/`rgb(243,244,246→ actually rendered
  text-gray-400 rgb(156,163,175) at rest, hover swaps to gray-100)` on real body bg:
  light inactive vs body 6.87:1; dark inactive vs body 6.99:1.
- Active tab text (wf-tab-active) vs body: light 5.71:1; dark 5.95:1.
- Hover text (`text-gray-700`/`dark:text-gray-100`, confirmed live via `page.hover()`):
  light 9.37:1; dark 16.12:1.
All ≥ 4.5:1 in both themes (point 7/12). axe's color-contrast rule also ran clean across
all 48 scan states in section 1, corroborating.
Note: LT-2026-09-07d already caught and fixed a spec-level contrast defect (originally
specified `text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-300`, 4.39:1, would have FAILED point 7) before
this attempt — the worker substituted the already-accepted What-If gray-600/400 pair
instead of guessing; that ruling is why the shipped code passes.

## 4. Point 11 — chart text alternative, panel isolation
`insights-panel-trends` (web/templates/pages/insights.html:161-172) still contains
`#chart-trends` immediately followed by `insights-trends-table`/`category-trends` inside
the SAME panel — byte-identical to master's inner markup (`git diff master` shows only the
tabpanel `<div>` wrapper added around the pre-existing card, confirmed against
`git show master:web/templates/pages/insights.html` lines 152-163). When another tab is
active, `insights-panel-trends.hidden === true` (native `hidden` attribute set by JS, not
`aria-hidden` — confirmed in section 2's Tab-key trace: hidden content is unreachable by
Tab and absent from axe's accessible-tree scans, which is why activating each tab and
re-running axe was necessary and found nothing).

## 5. Point 16 — JS-disabled parity
`node nojs.js` (Playwright context `javaScriptEnabled: false`) against the live server:
all 5 `[role="tabpanel"]` elements report `display: "block"`, `hasAttribute('hidden') ===
