render_insights_lt6_test.go's static assertions (`go test -run
TestRenderInsightsSupportingTabs -v` → PASS: no `hidden` attribute, no
`aria-selected="true"` in server output). Confirms progressive enhancement: JS off ⇒ every
panel visible, no assistive-tech state contradicts the visual page.

## 6. Point 10 — HTMX swap + tab persistence
`node htmxswap.js`: activated the Anomalies tab (persisted to
`localStorage['insightsActiveTab']`), then clicked the "2M" preset button, which triggers
the PRE-EXISTING `hx-get="/insights" hx-target="#insights-wrapper" hx-swap="outerHTML"`
form submit (insights.html:6-8, not owned by or modified by LT6). After the swap:
`aria-selected="true"` was on `insights-tab-anomalies` again (tab state correctly
re-applied via insights.js's `htmx:afterSwap` listener, web/static/js/insights.js:387-393)
and `localStorage` still read `"anomalies"`. Focus landed on the newly-rendered preset
button itself (a sensible, visible, operable control inside the swapped region) —
consistent with htmx's own focus-preservation on outerHTML swaps, which is pre-existing
platform/framework behaviour, not something LT6 wrote. OBSERVATION, not a FAIL: LT6 did
not change the swap mechanism or make focus handling worse; it added the one piece of new
behavior (tab-state re-application) and that piece worked correctly.

